WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.357 --> 00:00:02.076
This is the Holdings page.

2
00:00:02.076 --> 00:00:04.389
The Overview gives you the headlines.

3
00:00:04.389 --> 00:00:08.177
Here, you go coin by coin: what you hold, what it's worth,

4
00:00:08.177 --> 00:00:11.703
and what the wider market looks like behind each one.

5
00:00:12.360 --> 00:00:15.741
Holdings has its own account picker, up here on the right.

6
00:00:15.741 --> 00:00:19.211
It starts on whatever you chose in the exchange selector,

7
00:00:19.211 --> 00:00:21.951
and changing it here only changes this page.

8
00:00:22.633 --> 00:00:25.110
Let's pick the Kraken account called Main.

9
00:00:25.110 --> 00:00:28.753
The cards and the table now cover just that one account.

10
00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:32.805
On All exchanges, a coin you hold in several places

11
00:00:32.805 --> 00:00:35.979
shows up once, with the amounts added together.

12
00:00:35.979 --> 00:00:37.747
Let's switch back to everything.

13
00:00:38.410 --> 00:00:40.700
The page doesn't reload on its own.

14
00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:46.179
If you've had it open for a while, the refresh button fetches your balances and prices again.

15
00:00:46.839 --> 00:00:49.555
Across the top are five summary cards.

16
00:00:49.555 --> 00:00:54.010
Total value is everything on the selected accounts, in dollars.

17
00:00:54.010 --> 00:00:58.930
Underneath, you can see how many coins that covers, and how much of it is cash.

18
00:00:59.624 --> 00:01:03.175
The twenty-four hour change adds up how much each position

19
00:01:03.175 --> 00:01:05.930
gained or lost in dollars over the last day.

20
00:01:05.930 --> 00:01:11.183
Below it, that move is shown as a percentage of what the portfolio was worth a day ago.

21
00:01:11.849 --> 00:01:16.646
Best today and worst today are the coins whose price rose the most and fell

22
00:01:16.646 --> 00:01:21.187
the most over the last day, with how much you hold of each in dollars.

23
00:01:21.874 --> 00:01:27.808
And Largest position is your biggest holding by value, with its share of the whole portfolio.

24
00:01:28.481 --> 00:01:32.740
Below the cards is every asset you hold, one row each.

25
00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.596
Price is the current price, followed by how much it has moved

26
00:01:36.596 --> 00:01:40.200
over the last twenty-four hours and the last seven days.

27
00:01:40.875 --> 00:01:44.008
The seven-day trend is a small chart of the week, so you

28
00:01:44.008 --> 00:01:47.141
can see the shape of the move, not just where it ended.

29
00:01:47.141 --> 00:01:52.075
It's green when the week finished level or higher, and red when it finished lower.

30
00:01:52.740 --> 00:01:54.751
Amount is how many coins you hold.

31
00:01:54.751 --> 00:01:58.120
Value is what they're worth in dollars, and the next column

32
00:01:58.120 --> 00:02:00.975
is that value as a share of your whole portfolio.

33
00:02:01.646 --> 00:02:05.245
Market cap is the value of every coin of that kind in

34
00:02:05.245 --> 00:02:08.777
existence, across the whole market, not just yours.

35
00:02:08.777 --> 00:02:13.897
The last column shows how far today's price sits below the coin's all-time high.

36
00:02:14.562 --> 00:02:17.996
Cash balances, like dollars, are listed too.

37
00:02:17.996 --> 00:02:21.493
They count toward your total and your percentages, but there's

38
00:02:21.493 --> 00:02:24.539
no market data for them, so those columns stay empty.

39
00:02:25.221 --> 00:02:28.921
The table starts out sorted by value, biggest first.

40
00:02:28.921 --> 00:02:31.767
Click any column heading to sort by it instead.

41
00:02:31.767 --> 00:02:34.772
The arrow shows which column is doing the sorting.

42
00:02:35.451 --> 00:02:40.148
Sorting by the twenty-four hour column puts today's strongest coins at the top.

43
00:02:40.148 --> 00:02:44.670
Click the same heading again to flip the order, and the weakest come first.

44
00:02:45.346 --> 00:02:48.448
Sorting by the asset name runs from A to Z.

45
00:02:48.448 --> 00:02:51.905
Every other column starts with the largest number first.

46
00:02:51.905 --> 00:02:55.767
Anything without a figure in that column, like a cash balance,

47
00:02:55.767 --> 00:02:59.192
sinks to the bottom rather than being counted as zero.

48
00:02:59.876 --> 00:03:03.297
Select any row for the full breakdown of that coin.

49
00:03:03.297 --> 00:03:04.640
Let's open Bitcoin.

50
00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:09.135
Rows work from the keyboard too: tab to one and press Enter.

51
00:03:09.813 --> 00:03:14.523
Your position comes first: how much you hold, what it's worth, its share of

52
00:03:14.523 --> 00:03:19.045
your portfolio, and how many dollars it gained or lost in the last day.

53
00:03:19.045 --> 00:03:23.779
Held on lists each account the coin sits on, and how much is in each one.

54
00:03:24.454 --> 00:03:29.768
Market size shows the coin's market cap and its rank, and its fully diluted valuation,

55
00:03:29.768 --> 00:03:34.896
which is what it would be worth if its maximum supply were already in circulation.

56
00:03:34.896 --> 00:03:36.811
Then the day's trading volume.

57
00:03:37.474 --> 00:03:42.594
Volume divided by market cap shows how much of the coin changes hands in a day,

58
00:03:42.594 --> 00:03:47.584
with a plain-English reading, from thinly traded up to very actively traded.

59
00:03:48.249 --> 00:03:52.031
Supply shows how many coins are circulating, how many have been

60
00:03:52.031 --> 00:03:55.752
issued, and the maximum that can ever exist, if there is one.

61
00:03:55.752 --> 00:03:59.091
The bar shows how much of that eventual supply is already

62
00:03:59.091 --> 00:04:02.255
out there, and the last line is your own share of it.

63
00:04:02.924 --> 00:04:07.753
Price history gives you the day's range, the all-time high and when it happened, how

64
00:04:07.753 --> 00:04:12.581
far the price is from it now, and how much it would need to rise to get back there.

65
00:04:12.581 --> 00:04:15.800
The all-time low is at the bottom, with its date.

66
00:04:16.463 --> 00:04:21.612
Momentum shows the price change over the last hour, day, week and month.

67
00:04:21.612 --> 00:04:25.921
The last line works out what your current holding would have been worth thirty days ago.

68
00:04:26.597 --> 00:04:31.893
The last block comes from Kraken's public market data, whichever exchanges you use.

69
00:04:31.893 --> 00:04:38.508
It's the trading pair's own record on Kraken: its highest and lowest prices since Kraken has data for

70
00:04:38.508 --> 00:04:45.058
it, the fifty-two week range, the smallest order Kraken accepts, and Kraken's maker and taker fees.

71
00:04:45.727 --> 00:04:50.584
To look at another coin, just select its row, and the breakdown switches over.

72
00:04:50.584 --> 00:04:52.978
When you're done, the cross closes it.

73
00:04:53.648 --> 00:04:56.723
Your balances and prices come from your exchanges.

74
00:04:56.723 --> 00:05:00.446
The market figures, like market cap, supply and all-time

75
00:05:00.446 --> 00:05:03.239
highs, come from CoinGecko's public data.

76
00:05:03.239 --> 00:05:06.892
Only the coin's ticker is sent, never your balances, and the

77
00:05:06.892 --> 00:05:10.606
figures are kept for ten minutes before being fetched again.

78
00:05:11.268 --> 00:05:14.970
If CoinGecko can't be reached, a notice at the top of the page

79
00:05:14.970 --> 00:05:18.492
tells you that you're seeing the last figures Cyrus saved.

80
00:05:18.492 --> 00:05:22.574
Your balances and prices still come live from the exchange.

81
00:05:23.243 --> 00:05:26.728
That's Holdings: the headline numbers, every coin side

82
00:05:26.728 --> 00:05:30.148
by side, and a full breakdown whenever you need one.

83
00:05:30.148 --> 00:05:32.595
Next, we'll look at your open orders.

